+/*
+ * iOS 18 (xnu-11215) userland queries the Exclaves state with sysctlbyname().
+ * apfs_boot_util (mount-phase-2, graft_exclaveos) does
+ *     sysctlbyname("kern.exclaves_status") -> failure: "failed to get exclaves
+ *     status", returns errno, and the boot task aborts ("ExclaveOS graft");
+ *     == 0xFF (EXCLAVES_STATUS_NOT_SUPPORTED): skip the ExclaveOS graft, success;
+ *     == 1 (EXCLAVES_STATUS_AVAILABLE): graft the ExclaveOS cryptex;
+ *     anything else: EINVAL-like failure ("invalid exclaves status").
+ * This kernel has no exclaves, so answer what xnu-11215 answers when it is
+ * built without CONFIG_EXCLAVES (as for A12 and older): exclaves_get_status()
+ * == EXCLAVES_STATUS_NOT_SUPPORTED and exclaves_get_boot_stage() ==
+ * EXCLAVES_BOOT_STAGE_NONE.
+ *
+ * kern.exclaves_relaxed_requirements and kern.exclaves_inspection_status are
+ * only defined under CONFIG_EXCLAVES in xnu-11215; they stay absent (ENOENT),
+ * which callers treat as "no requirement relaxed".
